{"Title":"An Act clarifying constitutional officer employers for collective bargaining purposes","BillNumber":"S1664","DocketNumber":"SD829","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"PRF0","Name":"Paul R. Feeney","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PRF0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T11:04:51.01"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"PRF0","Name":"Paul R. Feeney","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PRF0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T11:04:51.01"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1664/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Feeney, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1664) of Paul R. Feeney for legislation to designate constitutional officers as employers of the employees under their jurisdiction.  Public Service.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. The definition of \"employee\" in Section 1 of Chapter 150E of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by striking out the words \"and the officers and employees within the departments of the state secretary, state treasurer, state auditor and attorney general\".\r\n\tSECTION 2. The definition of \"employer\" in Section 1 of Chapter 150E of the General Laws, as so appearing, is hereby amended by adding the following sentence:- \r\n\tIn the case of employees of the state secretary, state treasurer, state auditor and attorney general, the employer shall be the state secretary, state treasurer, state auditor and attorney general respectively.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J23","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J23"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}